From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ned <github@edoardo.fyi>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 04:39:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 099/104] runtime: reuse VU1 packet staging buffers

Reuse packet-vector capacity across native dispatches without changing the transactional state/data/GIF commit. Full data-memory staging remains necessary for failed-native fallback; reset only the active packet count. PS2X_VU1_STAGING=legacy restores per-call allocation. Differential mode exercises the pool, with a regression covering success/failure/shrinking/empty packet sequences.

Measured iPhone A13, venue=3 match autopilot, device A/B two pairs x 120 s (vu1-copy-cost-staging):
- fps 56.347 -> 57.928, +1.581 (control noise 0.783).
- late frames >18 ms 28.464% -> 16.945%, -11.519 pp (noise 10.275 pp).
- cpu_game_ms p50/p95 11.700/17.198 -> 11.627/15.776, -0.072/-1.422 ms (noise 0.493/0.610 ms).
- vu1_ms p50/p95 6.976/10.487 -> 6.934/10.036, -0.042/-0.451 ms (noise 0.928/0.180 ms); p50 unchanged within noise.
- GPU p50 2.605 -> 2.646 ms (+0.041, noise 0.135); process 1.425 -> 1.446 cores (+0.021, below 0.05 materiality).
- Gameplay/run underruns 0 -> 0; thermal maximum medians 0.5 -> 0 (noise 1).

Keep: counted smoothness and tail-time improvements with no counted regression. Present p99 and VU1 p50 remain within control noise; no claim of lower average worker CPU.
Validated build, quick/full tests, legacy tests, native/interpreter compare 320767 calls with zero mismatches/budget stops; macOS on/off each 60 fps and zero underruns. macOS package installed. A/B: build/device-ab/20261023T022011Z-vu1-copy-cost-staging/ab.txt.

